{
  "schema": 1,
  "books": {
    "opening": {
      "title": "Before the ninth night",
      "before": "p_bay",
      "music": {
        "file": "res://assets/audio/music/prologue-theme.mp3",
        "bar": 0
      },
      "end_bar": 20,
      "panels": [
        {
          "bar": 0,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/campaign/rooms/c1_pier.webp",
          "from": [
            0.42,
            0.56,
            1.0
          ],
          "to": [
            0.56,
            0.48,
            1.12
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 0.25,
              "text": "Bellwether. A fishing town on the Pacific coast.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 4.9
            },
            {
              "bar": 1.497,
              "text": "Six thousand people, one radio station, and a lot of fog.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 5.35
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bar": 3.5,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/campaign/rooms/c10_station.webp",
          "from": [
            0.5,
            0.55,
            1.14
          ],
          "to": [
            0.6,
            0.45,
            1.02
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 3.75,
              "text": "I’m Steve Mercer. For twelve years I ran the night shift at KBWR, the town radio station.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 6.95
            },
            {
              "bar": 5.731,
              "text": "Nobody hears the night engineer. The night engineer hears everything.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 5.95
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bar": 7.5,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/campaign/rooms/c5_shack.webp",
          "from": [
            0.35,
            0.6,
            1.1
          ],
          "to": [
            0.45,
            0.55,
            1.0
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 7.75,
              "text": "My dad, Frank, taught me how to listen. Every sound has a source, he used to say. Go and find it.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 7.35
            },
            {
              "bar": 8.83,
              "text": "Ham radio, every night. Strangers from all over the world, all of them his friends.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 6.65
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bar": 11.0,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/rooms/meeting.png",
          "from": [
            0.5,
            0.45,
            1.0
          ],
          "to": [
            0.5,
            0.5,
            1.12
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 11.25,
              "text": "My mom, Helen, was an interpreter. Government work, rooms with no windows. She never talked about it.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 7.55
            },
            {
              "bar": 13.695,
              "text": "She could hear what people meant, even when they said something else.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 5.95
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bar": 15.5,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/rooms/bay.png",
          "from": [
            0.5,
            0.42,
            1.0
          ],
          "to": [
            0.5,
            0.5,
            1.16
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 15.75,
              "text": "Eighteen months ago, they rowed out into the bay after dark. They said the water was making a sound.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 7.5
            },
            {
              "bar": 17.716,
              "text": "They asked me to come along.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 3.9
            },
            {
              "bar": 18.318,
              "text": "I said no. I had a shift.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 3.75
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "aftermath": {
      "title": "Eighteen months",
      "before": "c1_flat",
      "music": {
        "file": "res://assets/audio/music/prologue-theme.mp3",
        "bar": 37,
        "continue": true
      },
      "end_bar": 54,
      "panels": [
        {
          "bar": 37,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/campaign/rooms/c8_beach.webp",
          "from": [
            0.5,
            0.5,
            1.12
          ],
          "to": [
            0.62,
            0.62,
            1.22
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 37.25,
              "text": "In the morning, their boat drifted back to shore. Empty.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 5.3
            },
            {
              "bar": 38.545,
              "text": "Dad’s radio was still on.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 3.75
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bar": 39.5,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/campaign/rooms/c1_escape.webp",
          "from": [
            0.55,
            0.5,
            1.0
          ],
          "to": [
            0.45,
            0.5,
            1.1
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 39.75,
              "text": "Nobody found them. That was eighteen months ago.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 4.9
            },
            {
              "bar": 40.909,
              "text": "Mom called me from the boat that night. I kept her voicemail on a cassette. Most nights I play it at three in the morning. I don’t know what I’m listening for.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 10.45
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bar": 43.0,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/campaign/wide/c5_station.webp",
          "from": [
            0.5,
            0.5,
            1.12
          ],
          "to": [
            0.5,
            0.45,
            1.0
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 43.25,
              "text": "A year ago a company called Halcyon Media bought KBWR.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 5.2
            },
            {
              "bar": 44.944,
              "text": "Three weeks ago they replaced me with a machine called DJ AutoRick. It reads yesterday’s weather.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 7.35
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bar": 47.0,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/campaign/inserts/c1_pier.webp",
          "from": [
            0.5,
            0.5,
            1.0
          ],
          "to": [
            0.6,
            0.45,
            1.14
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 47.25,
              "text": "And then there’s Nora. Nora Reyes runs the animals at the aquarium and argues with everybody, me included.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 7.8
            },
            {
              "bar": 49.565,
              "text": "After the boat I went quiet. She pushed, then shouted, then stopped. Lately she’s been endlessly patient with me. I figured I’d worn her out.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 9.55
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bar": 51.0,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/title.webp",
          "from": [
            0.74,
            0.4,
            1.62
          ],
          "to": [
            0.5,
            0.5,
            1.0
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 51.25,
              "text": "So now I’m home in the mornings, with Dad’s old tape recorder and nothing left to fix.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 6.8
            },
            {
              "bar": 51.25,
              "text": "This is the story of how I started counting nights.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 5.05
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "after": {
      "title": "After the ninth night",
      "before": "one_year",
      "music": {
        "file": "res://assets/audio/music/prologue-theme.mp3",
        "bar": 31,
        "continue": true
      },
      "end_bar": 54,
      "panels": [
        {
          "bar": 31,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/campaign/rooms/epilogue.webp",
          "from": [
            0.45,
            0.5,
            1.0
          ],
          "to": [
            0.55,
            0.5,
            1.12
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 31.25,
              "text": "Before the ship left, the Choir gave the copies one last gift. They don’t need the ninth night anymore.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 7.65
            },
            {
              "bar": 33.497,
              "text": "More than two hundred of them stayed. Bellwether has a lot of new neighbors with familiar faces.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 7.3
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bar": 36.0,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/campaign/inserts/c1_pier.webp",
          "from": [
            0.55,
            0.45,
            1.12
          ],
          "to": [
            0.45,
            0.5,
            1.0
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 36.25,
              "text": "Iris chose a face of her own. People still say hello to the wrong Steve sometimes. We both say hello back.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 7.8
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bar": 39.5,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/campaign/rooms/c5_shack.webp",
          "from": [
            0.45,
            0.55,
            1.0
          ],
          "to": [
            0.35,
            0.6,
            1.12
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 39.75,
              "text": "Mom and Dad came home. Dad is back on the radio every Thursday.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 5.65
            },
            {
              "bar": 41.204,
              "text": "Dad labels everything now. The paint, the radios, me.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 5.15
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bar": 43.5,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/title.webp",
          "from": [
            0.72,
            0.46,
            1.6
          ],
          "to": [
            0.75,
            0.38,
            1.72
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 43.75,
              "text": "I don’t play the old voicemail anymore.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 4.45
            },
            {
              "bar": 44.611,
              "text": "The ring isn’t in the sock drawer anymore. Ask Nora where it is.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 5.7
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bar": 47.5,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/campaign/rooms/one_year.webp",
          "from": [
            0.4,
            0.5,
            1.12
          ],
          "to": [
            0.55,
            0.45,
            1.0
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 47.75,
              "text": "KBWR has live hosts again. Two of them.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 3.65
            },
            {
              "bar": 49.017,
              "text": "Stephen and I still argue about which one of us is the upgrade.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 3.772
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bar": 50.5,
          "image": "res://assets/illustrated/campaign/films/one_year.webp",
          "from": [
            0.5,
            0.55,
            1.0
          ],
          "to": [
            0.62,
            0.42,
            1.15
          ],
          "lines": [
            {
              "bar": 50.75,
              "text": "One year after the ninth night, a package arrived at the station.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 3.867
            },
            {
              "bar": 52.085,
              "text": "From very, very far away.",
              "narration": "",
              "seconds": 2.963
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
